# 3. Docker Image Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docker --version` | Displays Docker version |
| `docker info` | Displays Docker system information |
| `docker pull nginx` | Downloads an image |
| `docker pull nginx:1.27` | Downloads a specific image version |
| `docker images` | Lists images |
| `docker image ls` | Lists images |
| `docker build -t myweb:v1 .` | Creates an image |
| `docker build --no-cache -t myweb:v1 .` | Builds without using cache |
| `docker image inspect myweb:v1` | Displays image details |
| `docker history myweb:v1` | Displays image build history |
| `docker tag myweb:v1 myweb:v2` | Creates another image tag |
| `docker rmi myweb:v1` | Removes an image |
| `docker image rm myweb:v1` | Removes an image |
| `docker image prune` | Removes dangling images |
| `docker image prune -a` | Removes unused images |
| `docker save -o myweb.tar myweb:v1` | Saves an image as TAR |
| `docker load -i myweb.tar` | Loads an image from TAR |

### Important command explanations

**Build without cache:**

```bash
docker build --no-cache -t myweb:v1 .
```

Forces Docker to rebuild without using cached layers.

**Inspect image:**

```bash
docker image inspect myweb:v1
```

Displays image ID, size, architecture and configuration.

**Image history:**

```bash
docker history myweb:v1
```

Displays image layers and build history.

**Tag image:**

```bash
docker tag myweb:v1 myweb:v2
```

Creates another tag pointing to the same image.

**Save image:**

```bash
docker save -o myweb.tar myweb:v1
```

**Load image:**

```bash
docker load -i myweb.tar
```

