# 4. Docker Container Commands

A container is an instance of an image.

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docker run nginx` | Creates and runs a container |
| `docker run -d nginx` | Runs in background |
| `docker run -d --name mynginx nginx` | Assigns a name |
| `docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx` | Maps ports |
| `docker ps` | Lists running containers |
| `docker ps -a` | Lists all containers |
| `docker stop mynginx` | Stops a container |
| `docker start mynginx` | Starts a stopped container |
| `docker restart mynginx` | Restarts a container |
| `docker pause mynginx` | Pauses a container |
| `docker unpause mynginx` | Resumes a container |
| `docker kill mynginx` | Immediately terminates a container |
| `docker rm mynginx` | Removes a stopped container |
| `docker rm -f mynginx` | Forcefully removes a container |
| `docker rename mynginx webserver` | Renames a container |
| `docker exec -it mynginx bash` | Opens Bash inside a container |
| `docker exec -it mynginx sh` | Opens shell inside a container |
| `docker logs mynginx` | Displays logs |
| `docker logs -f mynginx` | Follows logs continuously |
| `docker inspect mynginx` | Displays container details |
| `docker stats` | Displays resource usage |
| `docker cp index.html mynginx:/usr/share/nginx/html/` | Copies host file into container |
| `docker cp mynginx:/usr/share/nginx/html/index.html .` | Copies container file to host |
| `docker top mynginx` | Displays running processes |
| `docker port mynginx` | Displays port mappings |
| `docker diff mynginx` | Displays filesystem changes |

### Important differences

| Command | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `docker stop` | Gracefully stops a container |
| `docker kill` | Immediately terminates a container |
| `docker rm` | Removes a container |
| `docker rmi` | Removes an image |
| `docker run` | Creates and starts a new container |
| `docker start` | Starts an existing stopped container |
| `docker exec` | Executes a command inside a running container |

