# 5. Docker Networking Commands

Docker networking allows containers to communicate with each other and external networks.

### Types of networks

| Network | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Bridge | Connects containers on the same Docker host |
| Host | Shares the host's network namespace |
| None | Disables normal network connectivity |
| Overlay | Connects containers across multiple Docker hosts |
| Macvlan | Gives containers their own MAC addresses |

### Networking commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docker network ls` | Lists networks |
| `docker network create mynetwork` | Creates a network |
| `docker network inspect mynetwork` | Displays network details |
| `docker network connect mynetwork myweb` | Connects a container |
| `docker network disconnect mynetwork myweb` | Disconnects a container |
| `docker network rm mynetwork` | Removes a network |
| `docker network prune` | Removes unused networks |
| `docker run -d --network bridge nginx` | Uses bridge networking |
| `docker run -d --network host nginx` | Uses host networking |
| `docker run -d --network none nginx` | Runs without normal networking |

**Example:**

```bash
docker network create mynetwork
docker network ls
docker network inspect mynetwork
docker network connect mynetwork myweb
docker network disconnect mynetwork myweb
docker network rm mynetwork
```

