# 9. Additional Docker Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docker attach container_name` | Attaches to the main process |
| `docker wait container_name` | Waits until the container stops |
| `docker update --restart=always container_name` | Updates restart policy |
| `docker context ls` | Lists Docker contexts |
| `docker compose version` | Checks Docker Compose version |
| `docker version` | Displays client and server versions |

### Docker restart policies

| Policy | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `no` | Never automatically restarts |
| `always` | Always restarts |
| `unless-stopped` | Restarts unless manually stopped |
| `on-failure` | Restarts if the container exits with an error |

Example:

```bash
docker run -d --restart=always --name myweb nginx
```

